s":[["tool-use","toolu_01U4Jqz8AvFyaxZVTjLLDq8H","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(shell-command->string \\\"git grep -n -l 'shell-command->string' -- docs | head -20\\\" \\\"/Users/svs/src/compos\\\")\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01U4Jqz8AvFyaxZVTjLLDq8H","\"docs/SCHEME-TEST-MIGRATION.md\\ndocs/WORKTREES.md\\n\"",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["tool-use","toolu_01CcRyU7WuoaYwj7ZdFgTnTU","mcp__compos__eval-scheme","{\"code\":\"(map (lambda (h) (list (plist-get h 'name) (plist-get h 'sig) (plist-get h 'doc))) (apropos \\\"http request\\\"))\"}"],["tool-result","toolu_01CcRyU7WuoaYwj7ZdFgTnTU","((\"receive an HTTP callback or webhook\" #f #f) (\"http-request\" \"(http-request URL [OPTS] [CALLBACK])\" \"the one primitive under all of these; OPTS is a plist of method, headers, params, body, json, form, timeout, connect-timeout, redirect and max-bytes\") (\"http-text\" \"(http-text URL [OPTS] [K])\" \"the body of URL as a string, or #f when the request failed\") (\"http-message\" \"(http-message REPLY)\" \"one readable line for a failure, or #f when the request succeeded\") (\"http-get\" \"(http-get URL [OPTS] [K])\" \"GET URL and answer (ok BOOL status N headers PLIST body STRING [json VALUE] [error TEXT]); with K the request runs off the lane and K gets the answer\") (\"http-error\" \"(http-error REPLY)\" \"why the request never reached a server, or #f\") (\"http-ok?\" \"(http-ok? REPLY)\" \"#t when the status was 2xx\") (\"http-patch\" \"(http-patch URL BODY [OPTS] [K])\" \"PATCH URL with BODY\") (\"http-head\" \"(http-head URL [OPTS] [K])\" \"the headers and status of URL, with no body\") (\"http-status\" \"(http-status REPLY)\" \"the HTTP status number, or #f when nothing answered\") (\"http-body\" \"(http-body REPLY)\" \"the response body as a string, always the bytes that arrived\") (\"google-request\" \"(google-request ACCOUNT SERVICE METHOD PATH PARAMS BODY CALLBACK)\" \"direct Google REST request; account is explicit.\") (\"http\" \"(http)\" \"M-x http — fetch a URL and show the status, the headers and the body in a buffer\") (\"http-delete\" \"(http-delete URL [OPTS] [K])\" \"DELETE URL\") (\"http-header\" \"(http-header REPLY NAME)\" \"one response header's value, by any capitalisation, or #f\") (\"http-post\" \"(http-post URL BODY [OPTS] [K])\" \"POST BODY to URL; a plist BODY is sent as JSON, a string BODY as its bytes\") (\"http-put\" \"(http-put URL BODY [OPTS] [K])\" \"PUT BODY to URL\") (\"http-download!\" \"(http-download! URL PATH [OPTS])\" \"write the body of URL to PATH; #t when it arrived\") (\"spreadsheet-app-request\" \"(spreadsheet-app-request BUFFER METHOD BODY)\" \"the isolated grid backend bridge\") (\"google-http!\" \"(google-http! ACCOUNT METHOD URL PARAMS BODY CALLBACK)\" \"authenticated Google HTTP transport.\") (\"http-json\" \"(http-json REPLY)\" \"the parsed JSON body, or #f when the body was not JSON\") (\"http-post-json\" \"(http-post-json URL BODY [OPTS] [K])\" \"the parsed JSON answer to a POST, or #f\") (\"fetch a URL\" #f #f) (\"google-request-mode\" #f \"Major mode\") (\"endpoint-ask\" \"(endpoint-ask NAME TEXT UNTIL [TIMEOUT] CB)\" \"send a query and collect the result frames up to the sentinel UNTIL; CB gets (OK FRAMES)\"))",false]],"role":"assistant"},{"blocks":[["text","Already committed and pushed — nothing was left uncommitted.\n\n```\n352f8b99  HTTP from Scheme: one http-request primitive over Req, and an http.scm client over it\n          apps/compos_core/lib/compos/core/scheme_api.ex\n          apps/compos_core/priv/packages/http.scm\n780510b1  init.scm + http.scm (load slot)\n```\n\n`apps/compos_core/priv/tests/http-test.scm` is tracked and in history too. `jj st` shows one modified file, `.compos/chats/1788987267-...chat`, which is this chat's own autosaved transcript, not work — I left it alone.\n\nOne correction to my earlier report: I said I added a docs entry. There is no docs/ markdown file for it. The documentation is the in-code registration, which `apropos` serves:\n\n```\n(http-request URL [OPTS] [CALLBACK])\n  the one primitive under all of these; OPTS is a plist of method, headers,\n  params, body, json, form, timeout, connect-timeout, redirect and max-bytes\n```\n\nAll 17 names resolve through `(apropos \"http request\")`. Say the word if you want a `docs/HTTP.md` as well."]],"role":"assistant"}]
